{"type":"message","id":"296a93d1","parentId":"f3da9bf4","timestamp":"2026-03-20T19:00:24.628Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[Fri 2026-03-20 19:00 UTC] [Subagent Context] You are running as a subagent (depth 1/2). Results auto-announce to your requester; do not busy-poll for status.\n\n[Subagent Task]: Write a bash script that checks if all ArgoCD applications are synced and healthy.\n\nRequirements:\n- Query the ArgoCD API (assume `argocd` CLI is available, or use raw HTTP to `/api/v1/applications`)\n- Output a summary table with columns: APP NAME, SYNC STATUS, HEALTH STATUS\n- Exit code 1 if any app is out of sync or unhealthy\n- Exit code 0 if all apps are synced and healthy\n- Handle authentication (token or server flag)\n- Make it production-ready with proper error handling\n\nSave as `check_argocd_health.sh` in the current directory."}],"timestamp":1774033224622}}
{"type":"message","id":"f6407339","parentId":"296a93d1","timestamp":"2026-03-20T19:01:05.894Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I need to create a bash script that checks ArgoCD application health and sync status. Let me write a production-ready script with proper error handling, authentication support, and a summary table output.\n</think>\n\nI'll create a production-ready bash script to check ArgoCD application health and sync status.\n\n<tool_call>\n<function=write>\n<parameter=path>\ncheck_argocd_health.sh\n</parameter>\n<parameter=content>\n#!/bin/bash\n#\n# check_argocd_health.sh - Check ArgoCD application sync and health status\n#\n# Usage: ./check_argocd_health.sh [OPTIONS]\n#\n# Options:\n#   --server <url>       ArgoCD server URL (default: https://argocd-server.default.svc.cluster.local:443)\n#   --token <token>      ArgoCD authentication token\n#   --insecure           Skip TLS certificate verification\n#   --output <format>    Output format: table (default), json, csv\n#   --all-namespaces     Check applications in all namespaces\n#   --namespace <ns>     Check only applications in specific namespace\n#   --app-name <name>    Check only specific application"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"vllm","model":"mlx-community/Qwen3.5-35B-A3B-4bit","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1774033224626}}
